<h1>Save (As)</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Command</span> <span class="Command">Save</span> <span lang="EN-GB">is accessible from</span> <i style="font-weight:bold;"><span class="Path" style="font-style:normal;">File &gt; Save</span><span lang="EN-GB">,</span> by pressing</i> <span class="Shortcut">Ctrl<b style="font-weight:normal;">+ S</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">, by pressing</span> <span class="Button">Save</span> <span lang="EN-GB">button on the toolbar or by choosing</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'Save'</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">button from the Arm menu.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">C</span>ommand Save As is accessible from <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>File &gt; Save As</b></span>.</p>
<p class="description"><span lang="EN-GB" class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Save</span> is a standard Windows command to save the current file. In KUBE all documents are saved with extension sab2.</p>
<p>If the current document is a new file (not preliminary saved), the standard Save As dialog will appear.</p>
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description</b></span>: Save As - standard Windows command to save the current file with a different name.</p>
